### Forms API: manual requests
### Works in Visual Studio, Rider and VS Code (REST Client). Start the API with `docker compose up -d --build`.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@form = leave-request

### 1. Create the form (version 1 becomes a draft)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/forms
Content-Type: application/json

< ../samples/leave-request.form.json

### 2. Try the draft schema before publishing
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/forms/{{form}}/validate?version=draft
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "employeeName": "Jane Doe", "leaveType": "other" } }

### 3. Publish version 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/forms/{{form}}/versions/draft/publish

### 4. Submit directly
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/forms/{{form}}/submissions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "data": {
    "employeeName": "Jane Doe",
    "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
    "leaveType": "annual",
    "startDate": "2026-12-21",
    "endDate": "2026-12-31",
    "workingDays": 7,
    "notify": ["manager", "team"]
  }
}

### 5. An invalid submission: every problem comes back with a code
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/forms/{{form}}/submissions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "employeeName": "J", "leaveType": "sick", "workingDays": 5, "salary": 1 } }

### 6. Autosave: start a draft. Copy the id and the ETag header from the response.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/forms/{{form}}/drafts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "data": { "employeeName": "Jane Doe", "leaveType": "sick" } }

### 7. Autosave: save again (replace the id and the ETag)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/drafts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "0"

{
  "data": {
    "employeeName": "Jane Doe",
    "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
    "leaveType": "sick",
    "startDate": "2026-11-02",
    "endDate": "2026-11-06",
    "workingDays": 5,
    "certificateNumber": "AB-123456"
  }
}

### 8. Autosave: submit the draft
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/drafts/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/submit

### 9. Version 2 removes a field: the response lists the change as breaking
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/forms/{{form}}/versions/draft
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schema": {
    "fields": [
      { "key": "employeeName", "label": "Full name", "type": "text", "required": true },
      { "key": "email", "label": "Work email", "type": "email", "required": true },
      { "key": "leaveType", "label": "Type of leave", "type": "select", "required": true,
        "options": [ { "value": "annual", "label": "Annual leave" }, { "value": "sick", "label": "Sick leave" } ] },
      { "key": "startDate", "label": "First day", "type": "date", "required": true },
      { "key": "endDate", "label": "Last day", "type": "date", "required": true },
      { "key": "workingDays", "label": "Working days", "type": "integer", "required": true }
    ]
  }
}

### 10. Publishing a breaking draft returns 409 ...
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/forms/{{form}}/versions/draft/publish

### 11. ... unless it is confirmed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/forms/{{form}}/versions/draft/publish?acceptBreakingChanges=true

### 12. Compare any two versions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/forms/{{form}}/versions/compare?from=1&to=2

### 13. Query submissions by content (JSONB containment, GIN index)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/forms/{{form}}/submissions?filter=%7B%22leaveType%22%3A%22annual%22%7D&limit=20
